 Client for `inventory-api`. Every function takes a `transport`,
 `async (request) => response`, so callers choose HTTP, IPC or a fake.
 
-- `listItems(transport)` → every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `listItems(transport)` → every item, ordered by `id`. It sends `GET /items`
+  with no cursor, then follows
+  `next_cursor` from each response, passing the cursor back unchanged, until
+  `next_cursor` is `null` or absent. A transport failure or a non-200 response
+  (including 400) on any page rejects the whole call; no partial list is
+  returned.
 - `getItem(transport, id)` → one item; rejects on any non-200 response.
 - `lowStock(items, threshold)` → SKUs with `qty` below the threshold.
 
